  "transcript": [
    {
      "approx_t": 0.0,
      "text": "What makes French men's faces so attractive?"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 3.0,
      "text": "Welcome to Beauty Across Borders, episode 25."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 5.0,
      "text": "Our country for today is France."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 7.0,
      "text": "The typical French man's face is built around a straight, fairly narrow nose"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 11.0,
      "text": "and deep-set eyes that sit under strong brows."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 13.5,
      "text": "The lips usually run medium full with a clear border rather than thin."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 17.5,
      "text": "And the hair does a lot of the work here. It tends to be wavy"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 20.0,
      "text": "and, in popular media at least, worn longer than the typical American cut,"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 23.5,
      "text": "which is why people said French American actor Timothée Chalamet was 'Americanized'"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 28.0,
      "text": "when he ditched the long curls."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 30.0,
      "text": "The French face tends to read as refined and a little seductive,"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 33.0,
      "text": "the classic loverboy impression."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 35.0,
      "text": "Louis Garrel captures it well, with soft dark features, expressive eyes, and longer hair"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 39.5,
      "text": "that leans romantic rather than tough."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 41.5,
      "text": "The same quality runs through many French faces—a kind of effortless nonchalance."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 45.5,
      "text": "The French population splits into six genetic clusters that follow its regions,"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 49.0,
      "text": "along a rough north-to-south gradient."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 51.0,
      "text": "That spread shows up in the faces too."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 53.0,
      "text": "In the north, you get the cooler, more refined look, seen in faces like Parisian Pierre Niney."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 58.0,
      "text": "That tends to give way to a warmer, more Mediterranean set of features in the south,"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 62.0,
      "text": "seen most clearly in Corsica, the home of model Baptiste Giabiconi."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 65.0,
      "text": "So there has never been a single French face."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 68.0,
      "text": "And this is even more true in 2026, as the country becomes increasingly cosmopolitan;"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 72.0,
      "text": "you can see all manner of aesthetics expressed on French men's faces, with roots ranging from sub-Saharan Africa"
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 77.0,
      "text": "and the Maghreb in the case of Kylian Mbappé, to Southeast Asia in the case of Bách Buquen."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 83.0,
      "text": "What ties them all together is their alluring charm."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 85.0,
      "text": "Leave a comment to let us know what country we should visit next."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 87.0,
      "text": "And if you want us to analyze your face, click the link in bio at Qoves.com."
    }
  ],
